-- s 38 def "insolvent under administration"
#ASSERT `kind of the definition of a term` "s 38" "insolvent under administration" FALSE EQUALS JUST VicMeans
#ASSERT `wording of the definition of a term` "s 38" "insolvent under administration" FALSE EQUALS JUST "—"
#ASSERT `members the definition of a term names` "s 38" "insolvent under administration" FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST "a person who is an undischarged bankrupt within the meaning of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 of the Commonwealth (or the corresponding provisions of the law of another jurisdiction)", "a person who has executed a deed of arrangement under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 of the Commonwealth (or the corresponding provisions of the law of another jurisdiction) if the terms of the deed have not been fully complied with", "a person whose creditors have accepted a composition under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 of the Commonwealth (or the corresponding provisions of the law of another jurisdiction) if a final payment has not been made under that composition", "a person for whom a debt agreement has been made under Part IX of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 of the Commonwealth (or the corresponding provisions of the law of another jurisdiction) if the debt agreement has not ended or has not been terminated", "a person who has executed a personal insolvency agreement under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 of the Commonwealth (or the corresponding provisions of the law of another jurisdiction) but not if the agreement has been set aside or terminated or all of the obligations that the agreement created have been discharged")
